{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013xJGRnoRKoi8aSGvzW9XfD","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"blast vibration simulation waveform \"not spectral matching\" OR \"distinct from\" OR \"unlike\" recorded history\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Full Waveform Prediction of Blasting Vibration Using Deep Learning\",\"url\":\"https://www.mdpi.com/2071-1050/14/13/8200\"},{\"title\":\"Final Report Role of blast design parameters on ground ...\",\"url\":\"https://files.dep.state.pa.us/Mining/BureauOfMiningPrograms/BMPPortalFiles/Blasting_Research_Papers/2005%20Adhikari%20Role%20of%20Blast%20Design.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Near-Field Blast Vibration Monitoring, Analysis and Modeling\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/392130103_Near-Field_Blast_Vibration_Monitoring_Analysis_and_Modeling\"},{\"title\":\"Simulation of Blasting Vibration Waveform based on Magnitude-phase Variation Law in Frequency Domain\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciopen.com/article/10.3963/j.issn.1001-487X.2025.04.017\"},{\"title\":\"Blasting Operations Using Different Initiation Methods in Deep   Underground Mines\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2006.02125\"},{\"title\":\"Research Review on Blast Vibration Intensity, Waveform and Spectrum: Prediction and Active Control\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciopen.com/article/10.3963/j.issn.1001-487X.2024.03.023\"},{\"title\":\"Motion parameter estimation and measured data correction derived from blast-induced vibration: New insights - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0263224118311047\"},{\"title\":\"Analysis of blasting vibration duration considering frequency and energy and its application - PMC\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11253058/\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, I found relevant information about blast vibration simulation and waveform analysis. Here are the key findings:\n\nThe common time-domain superposition method has limitations in accurately controlling spectrum characteristics, and the simulation research of frequency-domain waveforms remains insufficient. This suggests that simulation approaches may differ from recorded historical data in their spectral characteristics.\n\nA study proposes an amplitude-phase joint waveform simulation method based on Fourier analysis to meet the needs of blasting vibration analysis and safety assessment. Compared to the time-domain superposition method, the frequency-domain magnitude-phase joint waveform simulation method can more accurately characterize the distribution and variation of waveform characteristics.\n\nAdditionally, a blast vibration model simulates the vibration amplitude attenuation and the waveform change over distance separately, with multiple sets of seed waveforms measured at a range of distances from signature holes used as input for the model.\n\nThe research demonstrates that simulation methods are being actively refined to better represent the complexities observed in recorded blast vibration data, particularly regarding how waveforms change with distance and frequency characteristics.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"571dab6f-93f8-46f1-b7c5-b688e09d8b63","uuid":"a14d9f63-161f-4b91-a58c-06d04e9bfaa9","timestamp":"2026-07-06T16:25:15.117Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"blast vibration simulation waveform \"not spectral matching\" OR \"distinct from\" OR \"unlike\" recorded history","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01Mub1MCQSNhfUVsSshuT7LE","content":[{"title":"Full Waveform Prediction of Blasting Vibration Using Deep Learning","url":"https://www.mdpi.com/2071-1050/14/13/8200"},{"title":"Final Report Role of blast design parameters on ground ...","url":"https://files.dep.state.pa.us/Mining/BureauOfMiningPrograms/BMPPortalFiles/Blasting_Research_Papers/2005%20Adhikari%20Role%20of%20Blast%20Design.pdf"},{"title":"(PDF) Near-Field Blast Vibration Monitoring, Analysis and Modeling","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/392130103_Near-Field_Blast_Vibration_Monitoring_Analysis_and_Modeling"},{"title":"Simulation of Blasting Vibration Waveform based on Magnitude-phase Variation Law in Frequency Domain","url":"https://www.sciopen.com/article/10.3963/j.issn.1001-487X.2025.04.017"},{"title":"Blasting Operations Using Different Initiation Methods in Deep   Underground Mines","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2006.02125"},{"title":"Research Review on Blast Vibration Intensity, Waveform and Spectrum: Prediction and Active Control","url":"https://www.sciopen.com/article/10.3963/j.issn.1001-487X.2024.03.023"},{"title":"Motion parameter estimation and measured data correction derived from blast-induced vibration: New insights - ScienceDirect","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0263224118311047"},{"title":"Analysis of blasting vibration duration considering frequency and energy and its application - PMC","url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11253058/"}]},"Based on the web search results, I found relevant information about blast vibration simulation and waveform analysis. Here are the key findings:\n\nThe common time-domain superposition method has limitations in accurately controlling spectrum characteristics, and the simulation research of frequency-domain waveforms remains insufficient. This suggests that simulation approaches may differ from recorded historical data in their spectral characteristics.\n\nA study proposes an amplitude-phase joint waveform simulation method based on Fourier analysis to meet the needs of blasting vibration analysis and safety assessment. Compared to the time-domain superposition method, the frequency-domain magnitude-phase joint waveform simulation method can more accurately characterize the distribution and variation of waveform characteristics.\n\nAdditionally, a blast vibration model simulates the vibration amplitude attenuation and the waveform change over distance separately, with multiple sets of seed waveforms measured at a range of distances from signature holes used as input for the model.\n\nThe research demonstrates that simulation methods are being actively refined to better represent the complexities observed in recorded blast vibration data, particularly regarding how waveforms change with distance and frequency characteristics."],"durationSeconds":6.566015208999976,"searchCount":1}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FhsVeZmkKUPWcxsH96PYdj","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"blast vibration \"vector peak sum\" OR \"resultant PPV\" OR \"component PPV\" damage criterion regulation standard ISEE ANSI\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Construction Vibration: PPV & BS 7385 | Sensorbee\",\"url\":\"https://www.sensorbee.com/guides/construction-vibration-monitoring-ppv-bs7385\"},{\"title\":\"Determination of Blast Vibrations Using Peak Particle ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.diva-portal.org/smash/get/diva2:1025939/FULLTEXT01.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Drawbacks of Blast Vibration Regulations\",\"url\":\"https://vulcanhammer.net/wp-content/uploads/2017/01/blst-crt.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"INTERNATIONAL SOCIETY FOR SOIL MECHANICS AND GEOTECHNICAL ENGINEERING\",\"url\":\"https://www.issmge.org/uploads/publications/1/45/06-technical-committee-09-tc203-33.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Building vibration I Measure I Standard I Criteria I Effects I PPV\",\"url\":\"https://svantek.com/applications/building-vibrations/\"},{\"title\":\"Vector Sum and PPV - Texcel\",\"url\":\"https://texcel.com.au/vector-sum-and-ppv/\"},{\"title\":\"Prediction of peak particle velocity using hybrid random forest approach\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC11680976/\"},{\"title\":\"Blast Vibration Criteria Selection\",\"url\":\"https://www.eweb.org/documents/Projects/Water%20Storage/Blast-Vibration-Criteria-Selection.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Ground Vibration Monitoring Standards and Methodology\",\"url\":\"https://groundvibrationmonitoring.com/ground-vibration-monitoring-standards-methodology/\"},{\"title\":\"Analysis of the Impact of ground vibration on the blast zone within\",\"url\":\"https://www.bio-conferences.org/articles/bioconf/pdf/2024/65/bioconf_btmic2024_01067.pdf\"}]\n\nI found search results relevant to blast vibration damage criteria and PPV measurement standards. Here's what the sources reveal:\n\n## Vector Peak Sum vs. Component PPV Measurements\n\nThe peak component particle velocity (PCPV) is the highest PPV recorded in any single axis, while some standards and consent conditions specify resultant PPV — the vector sum of simultaneous components across all three axes — which always gives a higher value than PCPV. In reporting, the maximum measurement of any of the three components is used rather than the resultant vector of all three components combined.\n\nThe magnitude of the vector particle velocity (Vector Sum) is the amplitude of the vector sum of three time-synchronised velocity components directly measured by an instrument, with the Peak Vector Sum Velocity reported as the peak value found by computing this for every point in the waveform.\n\n## Damage Criteria and Standards\n\nAt present, there is no universally accepted standard for safe ground vibrations, though International Standard ISO 4866 refers to some major regulations of ground vibrations for different types of buildings. The criterion for structural damage of residential buildings was set at 51 mm/s (2 in/s) peak particle velocity in the frequency range of 3-100 Hz.\n\nThe \"ISEE Field Practices for Blasting Seismographs 2015\" was developed by the International Society of Explosives Engineers. Safe levels of ground vibration from blasting range from 0.5 to 2.0 in/sec peak particle velocity for residential-type structures.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"571dab6f-93f8-46f1-b7c5-b688e09d8b63","uuid":"186618bc-bb29-4e07-9bcf-ec90b02a9d8e","timestamp":"2026-07-06T16:25:17.119Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"blast vibration \"vector peak sum\" OR \"resultant PPV\" OR \"component PPV\" damage criterion regulation standard ISEE ANSI","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01HsVscKoprMBWmHgFVRm7uw","content":[{"title":"Construction Vibration: PPV & BS 7385 | Sensorbee","url":"https://www.sensorbee.com/guides/construction-vibration-monitoring-ppv-bs7385"},{"title":"Determination of Blast Vibrations Using Peak Particle ...","url":"https://www.diva-portal.org/smash/get/diva2:1025939/FULLTEXT01.pdf"},{"title":"Drawbacks of Blast Vibration Regulations","url":"https://vulcanhammer.net/wp-content/uploads/2017/01/blst-crt.pdf"},{"title":"INTERNATIONAL SOCIETY FOR SOIL MECHANICS AND GEOTECHNICAL ENGINEERING","url":"https://www.issmge.org/uploads/publications/1/45/06-technical-committee-09-tc203-33.pdf"},{"title":"Building vibration I Measure I Standard I Criteria I Effects I PPV","url":"https://svantek.com/applications/building-vibrations/"},{"title":"Vector Sum and PPV - Texcel","url":"https://texcel.com.au/vector-sum-and-ppv/"},{"title":"Prediction of peak particle velocity using hybrid random forest approach","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC11680976/"},{"title":"Blast Vibration Criteria Selection","url":"https://www.eweb.org/documents/Projects/Water%20Storage/Blast-Vibration-Criteria-Selection.pdf"},{"title":"Ground Vibration Monitoring Standards and Methodology","url":"https://groundvibrationmonitoring.com/ground-vibration-monitoring-standards-methodology/"},{"title":"Analysis of the Impact of ground vibration on the blast zone within","url":"https://www.bio-conferences.org/articles/bioconf/pdf/2024/65/bioconf_btmic2024_01067.pdf"}]},"I found search results relevant to blast vibration damage criteria and PPV measurement standards. Here's what the sources reveal:\n\n## Vector Peak Sum vs. Component PPV Measurements\n\nThe peak component particle velocity (PCPV) is the highest PPV recorded in any single axis, while some standards and consent conditions specify resultant PPV — the vector sum of simultaneous components across all three axes — which always gives a higher value than PCPV. In reporting, the maximum measurement of any of the three components is used rather than the resultant vector of all three components combined.\n\nThe magnitude of the vector particle velocity (Vector Sum) is the amplitude of the vector sum of three time-synchronised velocity components directly measured by an instrument, with the Peak Vector Sum Velocity reported as the peak value found by computing this for every point in the waveform.\n\n## Damage Criteria and Standards\n\nAt present, there is no universally accepted standard for safe ground vibrations, though International Standard ISO 4866 refers to some major regulations of ground vibrations for different types of buildings. The criterion for structural damage of residential buildings was set at 51 mm/s (2 in/s) peak particle velocity in the frequency range of 3-100 Hz.\n\nThe \"ISEE Field Practices for Blasting Seismographs 2015\" was developed by the International Society of Explosives Engineers. Safe levels of ground vibration from blasting range from 0.5 to 2.0 in/sec peak particle velocity for residential-type structures."],"durationSeconds":8.904605125000002,"searchCount":1}}
